add('decisions', 'Two phone plans fit my needs. Plan A costs $35 monthly with a $90 setup charge; Plan B costs $44 monthly with no setup charge. I will stay exactly 12 months and there are no taxes or exit fees. What is Plan A\'s total 12-month cost? Compare it with Plan B and mention nonprice factors.', 'A $510 versus B $528; A saves $18; coverage/service/contract matter.', 'sum', ['420','90'])
add('decisions', 'My usable car needs a $1,100 repair. A salesperson says a replacement only costs $240 monthly, but has not told me the down payment, term, APR, insurance change or final payment. How should I compare the choices without assuming the cheap monthly payment wins?', 'Total ownership and financing costs, independent repair assessment and reliability; missing details prevent firm conclusion; affordability and transport need.')
add('decisions', 'A new job pays $350 more take-home monthly, but commuting adds $120 and childcare adds $175 monthly. What monthly cash improvement remains? Help me consider the extra 45 minutes of travel each workday without assigning it an invented dollar value.', 'Net $55; time/stress/career and benefit changes; stated costs only.', 'subtract', ['350','120','175'])
add('decisions', 'A store offers a $480 appliance in four equal zero-interest payments, no fees if paid on time. What is each payment? I have $520 in my account but rent is due tomorrow. Explain why equal installments do not establish affordability.', 'Each $120; upcoming rent and total commitments matter, verify late fees, no false free-money framing.', 'divide', ['480','4'])
